    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Synthesis Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech as my SSML synthesis provider. It seems well-suited for this task. I'm now planning the structure of the Python script to use its API.\n\n\n**Defining the Synthesis Script**\n\nOkay, I'm firming up the structure for the `synthesize_ssml.py` script. The Google Cloud Text-to-Speech library is going to be my workhorse. I'm focusing on the core components now: importing the library, setting up the client, crafting the SSML with voice and prosody, configuring the audio output, and calling the `synthesize_speech` API. The `write` tool will take care of creating the file once I'm ready.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861877790,
          "start": 1789861874263
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc14ca570015lFU3nO0NAFIPG",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc14c5aa001sZGyIdFJ5rI7X6",
      "session_id": "ses_f43eb3a67ffea3LvWlhh28zaNf",
      "time_created": 1789861874263,
      "time_updated": 1789861877791
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "BG2CklMrt9XNDeNl",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\n\ndef synthesize_ssml(ssml_text, output_filename):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls.\"\"\"\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    input_text = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(ssml=ssml_text)\n\n    # Select the voice and audio file type\n    # You can find a list of supported voices and languages here:\n    # https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/docs/voices\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        name=\"en-US-Wavenet-D\",  # Example: a Wavenet voice\n        ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL,\n    )\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want to return\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    # Perform the text-to-speech request\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=input_text, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    # Write the response audio content to the output file.\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example SSML text with prosody controls\n    # You can adjust rate, pitch, and volume as needed.\n    # See more SSML tags here: https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/docs/ssml\n    example_ssml = \"\"\"\n    <speak>\n      <prosody rate=\"slow\" pitch=\"+2st\">\n        Hello there! This is an example of SSML synthesis.\n      </prosody>\n      <break time=\"1s\"/>\n      <prosody volume=\"+6dB\">\n        I can speak louder and with a different pace.\n      </prosody>\n    </speak>\n    \"\"\"\n    synthesize_ssml(example_ssml, \"output_ssml.mp3\")\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_ssml.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-im93xys2/synthesize_ssml.py",
            "truncated": false
          },
